window.CARDS=window.CARDS||{};CARDS["people-yamauchi-haruki"]=[{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v1-p34-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"yamauchi-haruki","q":"yamauchi haruki classroom day 1  the fabricated athletic record class 1 d classroom during hirata s introductions  following inogashira  steps forward smoothly to deliver his introduction   i m yamauchi haruki  i competed in table tennis during elementary school  and in junior high i was the ace player on our baseball team  i was number four  i got hurt during the inter high school championships  though  and i m undergoing rehab now  nice to meet you  habitual bluffer and exaggerator  invents grandiose athletic credentials to impress classmates  unaware that claiming to have played in the  inter high school championships   a high school exclusive tournament  while in junior high exposes his lie immediately  talkative and easily carried away  boastful  overly detailed self aggrandizement","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v1-p34-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Classroom Day 1: the fabricated athletic record<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.34<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Class 1-D classroom during Hirata&#x27;s introductions, following Inogashira.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’m Yamauchi Haruki. I competed in table tennis during elementary school, and in junior high I was the ace player on our baseball team. I was number four. I got hurt during the inter-high school championships, though, and I’m…”<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Steps forward smoothly to deliver his introduction.<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m Yamauchi Haruki. I competed in table tennis during elementary school, and in junior high I was the ace player on our baseball team. I was number four. I got hurt during the inter-high school championships, though, and I’m undergoing rehab now. Nice to meet you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Habitual bluffer and exaggerator; invents grandiose athletic credentials to impress classmates, unaware that claiming to have played in the &quot;inter-high school championships&quot; (a high school exclusive tournament) while in junior high exposes his lie immediately. Talkative and easily carried away.<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Voice<\/span> Boastful, overly detailed self-aggrandizement.<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v1-p68-1\">→ After: Club fair browsing with Sudō and Ike<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v1-p68-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action","w":"ike-kanji sudou-ken yamauchi-haruki","q":"yamauchi haruki club fair browsing with sudo and ike gymnasium club fair  accompanies sudo and ike as part of their trio  follows ike around the gym looking for fun and girls  participates in bringing ayanokoji into the boys  group chat network  natural comedic partner to ike  aligned in chasing girls and avoiding hard work  close peer within the forming male clique","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v1-p68-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Club fair browsing with Sudō and Ike<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.68–71<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Gymnasium club fair. Accompanies Sudō and Ike as part of their trio.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q action\">Follows Ike around the gym looking for fun and girls; participates in bringing Ayanokōji into the boys&#x27; group chat network.<span class=\"pg\">p.68–71<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Natural comedic partner to Ike; aligned in chasing girls and avoiding hard work.<span class=\"pg\">p.68–71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Close peer within the forming male clique.<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v1-p34-1\">← Before: Classroom Day 1: the fabricated athletic record<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v1-p72-1\">→ After: Conspiring with Ike on the swimsuit bet<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v1-p72-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action","w":"ike-kanji yamauchi-haruki","q":"yamauchi haruki conspiring with ike on the swimsuit bet classroom 1 d morning before swimming  arrives early with ike  eagerly discussing the girls  upcoming appearance in swimsuits  actively assists in recruiting classmates into the betting pool run by sotomura  partner in crime in teenage boy antics","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v1-p72-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Conspiring with Ike on the swimsuit bet<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.72–75<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Classroom 1-D morning before swimming.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q action\">Arrives early with Ike, eagerly discussing the girls&#x27; upcoming appearance in swimsuits; actively assists in recruiting classmates into the betting pool run by Sotomura.<span class=\"pg\">p.72–75<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Partner-in-crime in teenage boy antics.<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v1-p68-1\">← Before: Club fair browsing with Sudō and Ike<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v1-p102-1\">→ After: Classroom disruption &amp; the 900 APEC blunder<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v1-p102-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"yamauchi-haruki","q":"yamauchi haruki classroom disruption   the 900 apec blunder named in class 1 d s  idiot trio  with ike and sudo  classroom 1 d  then keyaki mall cafe  disrupts second period math laughing loudly with ike  established as part of the  idiot trio  attempts to defend his intellect by delivering an absurd  fabricated academic claim   huh  i ll have you know that i scored 900 points on the apec   you don t even know  it s a super tough test for english  when kushida points out that apec is the asia pacific economic cooperation forum and asks if he meant the toeic english test  yamauchi stumbles and tries to bluff his way through  th they re related though  aren t they  shameless braggart with remarkably low general knowledge  invents claims out of thin air that immediately collapse under basic scrutiny","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v1-p102-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Classroom disruption &amp; the 900 APEC blunder<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.102, 118<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Classroom 1-D; then Keyaki Mall café.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Huh? I’ll have you know that I scored 900 points on the APEC.”<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You don’t even know? It’s a super tough test for English.”<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Post<\/span> Named in Class 1-D’s “Idiot Trio” with Ike and Sudō.<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Disrupts second-period math laughing loudly with Ike; established as part of the &quot;Idiot Trio&quot;.<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Attempts to defend his intellect by delivering an absurd, fabricated academic claim.<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> When Kushida points out that APEC is the Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation forum and asks if he meant the TOEIC English test, Yamauchi stumbles and tries to bluff his way through (*“Th-they’re related though, aren’t they?”*).<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Shameless braggart with remarkably low general knowledge; invents claims out of thin air that immediately collapse under basic scrutiny.<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v1-p72-1\">← Before: Conspiring with Ike on the swimsuit bet<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v1-p120-1\">→ After: 0-point bankruptcy &amp; pawning the game console<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v1-p120-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka yamauchi-haruki","q":"yamauchi haruki 0 point bankruptcy   pawning the game console classroom 1 d  may 1st morning homeroom and lunch break  exchanges bewildered glances with hondou when no monthly points arrive  wails in theatrical  incredible agony upon realizing class d received zero points  having completely drained his initial 100 000 points in april  academic failure  scores in the red on the short test  placed on the list of seven students facing immediate expulsion at midterms  suddenly appears from under ayanokoji s desk  expression deathlike  to pawn off his handheld video game console   hey  buy this from me for 20 000 points  i can t buy anything   cried   how the heck should i know  come on  it s good  right  it s special  so it s a good deal  outraged when ayanokoji counters with a ruthless offer of just 1 000 points  goes teary eyed  grossing ayanokoji out   ayanokouji  come on  you re my only hope  realizing ayanokoji isn t biting  immediately switches targets to sotomura  the professor    shamelessly raising the ask price to 22 000 points   professor  your best buddy has a favor to ask  buy this game system for 22 000 points  shameless hustler  tries to exploit friendship for personal financial rescue  panics under immediate monetary stress  targets him as an easy mark for pawning goods  only to be shut down by ak s hardball bargaining","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v1-p120-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">0-point bankruptcy &amp; pawning the game console<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.120, 126, 128, 137–138<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Classroom 1-D, May 1st morning homeroom and lunch break.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Hey, buy this from me for 20,000 points. I can’t buy anything!” (cried)<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“How the heck should I know? Come on, it’s good, right? It’s special, so it’s a good deal.”<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Ayanokouji! Come on, you’re my only hope!”<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Exchanges bewildered glances with Hondou when no monthly points arrive.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Wails in theatrical, incredible agony upon realizing Class D received zero points, having completely drained his initial 100,000 points in April.<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Academic failure: scores in the red on the short test, placed on the list of seven students facing immediate expulsion at midterms.<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Suddenly appears from under Ayanokōji’s desk, expression deathlike, to pawn off his handheld video game console.<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Outraged when Ayanokōji counters with a ruthless offer of just 1,000 points; goes teary-eyed, grossing Ayanokōji out.<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Realizing Ayanokōji isn’t biting, immediately switches targets to Sotomura (“The Professor”) — shamelessly raising the ask price to 22,000 points.<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Professor! Your best buddy has a favor to ask! Buy this game system for 22,000 points!”<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Shameless hustler; tries to exploit friendship for personal financial rescue; panics under immediate monetary stress.<span class=\"pg\">p.137–138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Targets him as an easy mark for pawning goods, only to be shut down by AK&#x27;s hardball bargaining.<span class=\"pg\">p.137–138<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v1-p102-1\">← Before: Classroom disruption &amp; the 900 APEC blunder<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v1-p153-1\">→ After: The quiet study group holdout<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v1-p153-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action","w":"yamauchi-haruki","q":"yamauchi haruki the quiet study group holdout one of the three failing students  with sudou and ike  who stays in his seat instead of joining hirata s announced study group  seems unsure for a moment  then remains seated with the others  agrees to attend horikita s study group via kushida s text recruitment  yamauchi kun and ike kun said okay   w b  shows up at the library session with ike  sudou  and okitani  silently starts putting his textbook away when ike quits  following the group out of the library without protest  passive follower of the idiot trio  goes along with whatever sudou and ike decide","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v1-p153-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The quiet study group holdout<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.153, 166–178<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q action\">One of the three failing students (with Sudou and Ike) who stays in his seat instead of joining Hirata&#x27;s announced study group; seems unsure for a moment, then remains seated with the others.<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q action\">Agrees to attend Horikita&#x27;s study group via Kushida&#x27;s text recruitment (&quot;Yamauchi-kun and Ike-kun said okay! (・w・)b&quot;).<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Shows up at the library session with Ike, Sudou, and Okitani.<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Silently starts putting his textbook away when Ike quits, following the group out of the library without protest.<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Passive follower of the Idiot Trio; goes along with whatever Sudou and Ike decide.<span class=\"pg\">p.153, 178<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v1-p120-1\">← Before: 0-point bankruptcy &amp; pawning the game console<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v1-p206-1\">→ After: Following Ike back into studying<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v1-p206-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"yamauchi-haruki","q":"yamauchi haruki following ike back into studying arrives with ike on cloud nine from kushida s invitation  nods along at ike s cram the night before plan  instantly takes ak s kushida bait and outbids ike for the date stakes   no  no  me  go on a date with me  i ll show you  i ll get fifty two points  pleased with early results  chemistry easier than expected   chemistry wasn t as hard as i thought it d be  either  pledges to try harder alongside ike after sudou s club break declaration   we re definitely gonna do this     yeah  me  too  pure follower momentum  peer incentives and group excitement carry him where personal stakes never would","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v1-p206-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Following Ike back into studying<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.206, 210–211, 218, 227<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“No, no, me! Go on a date with me! I’ll show you! I’ll get fifty-two points!”<span class=\"pg\">p.210<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Chemistry wasn’t as hard as I thought it’d be, either.”<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“We’re definitely gonna do this!” / “Yeah! Me, too!”<span class=\"pg\">p.227<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Arrives with Ike on cloud nine from Kushida&#x27;s invitation; nods along at Ike&#x27;s cram-the-night-before plan.<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Instantly takes AK&#x27;s Kushida bait and outbids Ike for the date stakes.<span class=\"pg\">p.210<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Pleased with early results: chemistry easier than expected.<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Pledges to try harder alongside Ike after Sudou&#x27;s club-break declaration.<span class=\"pg\">p.227<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Pure follower momentum: peer incentives and group excitement carry him where personal stakes never would.<span class=\"pg\">p.210–227<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v1-p153-1\">← Before: The quiet study group holdout<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v1-p236-1\">→ After: Old-test euphoria &amp; shock<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v1-p236-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"yamauchi-haruki","q":"yamauchi haruki old test euphoria   shock laugh complains about the sunk cost of studying when the old papers appear   what the hell  if we had these  then wasn t it pointless to study so hard   laughing  grinning alongside ike  reviewing the old papers at the break  stunned with ike at horikita s apology","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v1-p236-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Old-test euphoria &amp; shock<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.236, 241, 245<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“What the hell? If we had these, then wasn’t it pointless to study so hard?” (laughing)<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Laugh-complains about the sunk cost of studying when the old papers appear.<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Grinning alongside Ike, reviewing the old papers at the break.<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Stunned with Ike at Horikita&#x27;s apology.<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v1-p206-1\">← Before: Following Ike back into studying<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v1-p246-1\">→ After: Results-day cheer<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v1-p246-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action","w":"yamauchi-haruki","q":"yamauchi haruki results day cheer stands and cheers with ike at sudou s scores  stays silent afterward  knowing comfort would backfire","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v1-p246-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Results-day cheer<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.246<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q action\">Stands and cheers with Ike at Sudou&#x27;s scores; stays silent afterward (knowing comfort would backfire).<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><\/ul><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v1-p236-1\">← Before: Old-test euphoria &amp; shock<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v1-p256-1\">→ After: The victory-party braggart<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v1-p256-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"spoken","w":"yamauchi-haruki","q":"yamauchi haruki the victory party braggart  all things considered  though  that midterm was dangerous  if we hadn t put the study group together  i would ve been fine  but ike and sudou would have definitely gotten kicked out   rewrites history   ike immediately counters that he was also near expulsion   no  no  i could have gotten a perfect score if i were serious about it  really   we tried so hard on the midterm that they ll definitely give us some points  right   then we re not getting any points next month  either  boo   after horikita s average score reality check   gladly   accepting the class a helper ask alongside ike  post crisis bravado  retcons his own expulsion risk into a sure thing   pure face saving","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v1-p256-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The victory-party braggart<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.256–261<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“All things considered, though, that midterm was dangerous. If we hadn’t put the study group together, I would’ve been fine, but Ike and Sudou would have definitely gotten kicked out.” (rewrites history — Ike immediately counters…”<span class=\"pg\">p.256<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“No, no, I could have gotten a perfect score if I were serious about it. Really.”<span class=\"pg\">p.256<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“We tried so hard on the midterm that they’ll definitely give us some points, right?!”<span class=\"pg\">p.258<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “All things considered, though, that midterm was dangerous. If we hadn’t put the study group together, I would’ve been fine, but Ike and Sudou would have definitely gotten kicked out.” (rewrites history — Ike immediately counters that he was also near expulsion)<span class=\"pg\">p.256<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Then we’re not getting any points next month, either. Boo.” (after Horikita&#x27;s average-score reality check)<span class=\"pg\">p.258<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Gladly!” (accepting the Class A helper ask alongside Ike)<span class=\"pg\">p.261<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Post-crisis bravado: retcons his own expulsion risk into a sure-thing — pure face-saving.<span class=\"pg\">p.256<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v1-p246-1\">← Before: Results-day cheer<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p19-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"","w":"yamauchi-haruki","q":"yamauchi haruki ch 2  2 2    2 4  crew member  key club member lunch ensemble   you ve got people like ike and yamauchi  who aren t very popular with girls  they eat with their group of guy friends  including sudou and hondou  almost every day  one of  the rest of us  who made duplicate keycards to ayanokoji s room and treat it as the group s meeting spot  sudou refuses to surrender his clone  still grouped with ike as the class s non popular boy clique two months in","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p19-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.2 &amp; §2.4: crew member, key-club member<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.19, p.27–28<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Lunch ensemble: &quot;you’ve got people like Ike and Yamauchi, who aren’t very popular with girls. They eat with their group of guy friends, including Sudou and Hondou, almost every day.&quot;<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> One of &quot;the rest of us&quot; who made duplicate keycards to Ayanokōji&#x27;s room and treat it as the group&#x27;s meeting spot; Sudou refuses to surrender his clone.<span class=\"pg\">p.27–28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Still grouped with Ike as the class&#x27;s non-popular boy clique two months in.<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p42-1\">→ After: Ch.3: one sentence from him undoes Kushida&#x27;s whole appeal<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p42-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"sudou-ken ike-kanji yamauchi-haruki","q":"yamauchi haruki ch 3  one sentence from him undoes kushida s whole appeal  hey  kushida chan  i just can t believe what sudou said  i think he lied so he could justify what he did  he talked about beating up kids all the time in junior high  he even told us how much fun it was to beat people up  he is the pivot of the homeroom  ak marks the turn as his    instantly  silence enveloped the classroom  the first to speak wasn t the eyewitness  but yamauchi  and  after yamauchi voiced his concerns  the rest of the class murmured their dissatisfaction with sudou in turn  at the cafeteria table he volunteers first for the case   i guess it s just up to us    sudou reads it as loyalty   i knew for sure you d understand  yamauchi  i m really counting on you too  ayanokouji  the same boy who supplies the class s proof that sudou is a habitual bully is then trusted as  one of us  when sudou needs helpers  ak notes the ranking his own name gets behind yamauchi s  his accusation is spoken to kushida by name and lands because the class already half believes it   he says out loud what sudou has bragged about to him and ike privately","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p42-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: one sentence from him undoes Kushida&#x27;s whole appeal<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.42–45<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At the cafeteria table he volunteers first for the case: “I guess it’s just up to us.” — Sudou reads it as loyalty: &quot;I knew for sure you’d understand, Yamauchi. I’m really counting on you too, Ayanokouji.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Hey, Kushida-chan. I just can’t believe what Sudou said. I think he lied so he could justify what he did. He talked about beating up kids all the time in junior high. He even told us how much fun it was to beat people up.”<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> He is the pivot of the homeroom: AK marks the turn as his — &quot;Instantly, silence enveloped the classroom. The first to speak wasn’t the eyewitness, but Yamauchi.&quot; and &quot;After Yamauchi voiced his concerns, the rest of the class murmured their dissatisfaction with Sudou in turn.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.42–43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> The same boy who supplies the class&#x27;s proof that Sudou is a habitual bully is then trusted as &quot;one of us&quot; when Sudou needs helpers; AK notes the ranking his own name gets behind Yamauchi&#x27;s.<span class=\"pg\">p.42, p.45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> His accusation is spoken to Kushida by name and lands because the class already half-believes it — he says out loud what Sudou has bragged about to him and Ike privately.<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p19-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.2 &amp; §2.4: crew member, key-club member<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p48-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.1: the other half of the crush council<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p48-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou horikita-suzune yamauchi-haruki","q":"yamauchi haruki ch 3  3 1  the other half of the crush council  no way  you seriously think she ll stoop to your level  ike   h hey  what are you fantasizing about  spill it    ak   apparently yamauchi couldn t stand the fact that ike could do as he pleased in his fantasies   damn it  i won t be outdone  i ve also thought of a few things   it would be best if kushida chan were my girlfriend  it would be the best if she were my girlfriend    ak counts the repetition   yamauchi said it twice  it must ve been important to him   but wait  since kushida chan is so cute  don t you think she ll get a boyfriend any day now    ike has to reply  don t say that  yamauchi   i see  i feel like i can imagine that  so cute    on sudou s fantasy horikita   yamauchi glanced at horikita and got lost in his delusional fantasies  competitive rather than romantic  his desire for kushida is measured against ike s and voiced as one upmanship  i won t be outdone  and he can transfer the same script onto horikita minutes after hearing sudou describe her  she is his stated girlfriend target  named twice in one breath  ak s pity for her is aimed at exactly this pair  he is lost in a horikita fantasy while she is  at that same table  refusing sudou outright   the gap between his version of her and the real one is the joke ak records","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p48-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 §3.1: the other half of the crush council<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.48–52<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“No way. You seriously think she’ll stoop to your level, Ike?”<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“H-hey, what are you fantasizing about?! Spill it!” — AK: &quot;Apparently Yamauchi couldn’t stand the fact that Ike could do as he pleased in his fantasies.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Damn it! I won’t be outdone! I’ve also thought of a few things!”<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It would be best if Kushida-chan were my girlfriend… It would be the best if she were my girlfriend…” — AK counts the repetition: &quot;Yamauchi said it twice. It must’ve been important to him.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But wait. Since Kushida-chan is so cute, don’t you think she’ll get a boyfriend any day now?” — Ike has to reply &quot;Don’t say that, Yamauchi!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see… I feel like I can imagine that. So cute.” — on Sudou&#x27;s fantasy Horikita: &quot;Yamauchi glanced at Horikita and got lost in his delusional fantasies.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Competitive rather than romantic: his desire for Kushida is measured against Ike&#x27;s and voiced as one-upmanship (&quot;I won’t be outdone&quot;), and he can transfer the same script onto Horikita minutes after hearing Sudou describe her.<span class=\"pg\">p.48–52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> She is his stated girlfriend target, named twice in one breath; AK&#x27;s pity for her is aimed at exactly this pair.<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> He is lost in a Horikita fantasy while she is, at that same table, refusing Sudou outright — the gap between his version of her and the real one is the joke AK records.<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p42-1\">← Before: Ch.3: one sentence from him undoes Kushida&#x27;s whole appeal<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p54-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.2–3.3: held in the classroom, then frozen in Class B<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p54-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"yamauchi-haruki","q":"yamauchi haruki ch 3  3 2 3 3  held in the classroom  then frozen in class b conscripted as the waiting crew while kushida chases horikita   okay  the boys chorused  in the doorway of class b   even ike and yamauchi appeared to be shaking in their boots  they simply stood frozen in the classroom doorway  unable to move     the pair  comrades in vexation  grasped each other s arms   don t panic  ike  it s okay  we re in kushida chan s class  so we re one step ahead of them  ak s measure of the pair in class b  the gap between them and the people kushida chats up is what they notice  not the witness list   no one was more jealous of this than ike and yamauchi  kushida was happily chatting with people who were clearly more attractive than they  he is asked to canvass and does stand in a doorway  no witness lead in chapter 3 is ever traced to him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p54-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 §3.2–3.3: held in the classroom, then frozen in Class B<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.54, p.61–63<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Conscripted as the waiting crew while Kushida chases Horikita: &quot;“Okay!” the boys chorused.&quot; In the doorway of Class B: &quot;Even Ike and Yamauchi appeared to be shaking in their boots. They simply stood frozen in the classroom doorway, unable to move.&quot; — &quot;The pair, comrades in vexation, grasped each other’s arms.&quot; AK&#x27;s measure of the pair in Class B: the gap between them and the people Kushida chats up is what they notice, not the witness list. &quot;No one was more jealous of this than Ike and Yamauchi. Kushida was happily chatting with people who were clearly more attractive than they.&quot;<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Don’t panic, Ike. It’s okay. We’re in Kushida-chan’s class, so we’re one step ahead of them!”<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> He is asked to canvass and does stand in a doorway; no witness lead in Chapter 3 is ever traced to him.<span class=\"pg\">p.54–63<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p48-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.1: the other half of the crush council<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p79-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.1: he has the only confident opinion of Sakura, and it is invented<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p79-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"sakura-airi yamauchi-haruki","q":"yamauchi haruki ch 4  4 1  he has the only confident opinion of sakura  and it is invented he is the one surprised by sudou s blankness about the girl who sits near him   yamauchi appeared quite surprised   can t we just go to sakura s room right now  we don t have much time    ak   i thought that yamauchi s proposal seemed innocuous  but it all came down to sakura s personality and behavior   she s plain  that s it  talk about a waste  man  like pearls before swine    ak s staging of the line   while yamauchi spoke  he gestured with his hands near his chest  to represent sakura s breasts   uh  ahh well  i may or may not have said something like that    cornered by ike s memory of a confession to sakura   n no  i wasn t  i wasn t lying  it was just a misunderstanding  it wasn t sakura  it was a girl from the next class over  not a gloomy and ugly girl like sakura  err  hold on  sorry  i got a message    ak   yamauchi dodged the question by whipping out his phone  he will say anything about a girl he has never spoken to and retract it in the same breath to stay socially safe  his cruelty is reflexive and his cowardice immediate  the volume s only claim that anyone ever confessed to her is a claim he withdraws under pressure   and the withdrawal describes her as  gloomy and ugly  while doing it","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p79-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.1: he has the only confident opinion of Sakura, and it is invented<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.79–82<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">He is the one surprised by Sudou&#x27;s blankness about the girl who sits near him: &quot;Yamauchi appeared quite surprised.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Can’t we just go to Sakura’s room right now? We don’t have much time.” — AK: &quot;I thought that Yamauchi’s proposal seemed innocuous, but it all came down to Sakura’s personality and behavior.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“She’s plain, that’s it. Talk about a waste, man. Like pearls before swine.” — AK&#x27;s staging of the line: &quot;While Yamauchi spoke, he gestured with his hands near his chest, to represent Sakura’s breasts.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Uh, ahh…well, I may or may not have said something like that.” — cornered by Ike&#x27;s memory of a confession to Sakura.<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “N-no, I wasn’t. I wasn’t lying. It was just a misunderstanding. It wasn’t Sakura; it was a girl from the next class over. Not a gloomy and ugly girl like Sakura. Err, hold on. Sorry, I got a message.” — AK: &quot;Yamauchi dodged the question by whipping out his phone.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> He will say anything about a girl he has never spoken to and retract it in the same breath to stay socially safe; his cruelty is reflexive and his cowardice immediate.<span class=\"pg\">p.81–82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> The volume&#x27;s only claim that anyone ever confessed to her is a claim he withdraws under pressure — and the withdrawal describes her as &quot;gloomy and ugly&quot; while doing it.<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p54-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.2–3.3: held in the classroom, then frozen in Class B<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p129-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.8, §4.11: he is a category in someone else&#x27;s phone etiquette<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p129-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"","w":"yamauchi-haruki","q":"yamauchi haruki ch 4  4 8   4 11  he is a category in someone else s phone etiquette he is ruled out of kushida s errand before it is offered   if she d invited ike or yamauchi along  they would have had eyes only for kushida  in the narrator s ranking of callers he is in the call back later tier   if it were ike or yamauchi  i d call them back later  but if it were horikita i d have to think about it  he has no scene of his own in the second half of chapter 4  both mentions are the class s assumptions about him rather than anything he does","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p129-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.8, §4.11: he is a category in someone else&#x27;s phone etiquette<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.129, p.148<\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> He is ruled out of Kushida&#x27;s errand before it is offered: &quot;If she’d invited Ike or Yamauchi along, they would have had eyes only for Kushida.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> In the narrator&#x27;s ranking of callers he is in the call-back-later tier: &quot;If it were Ike or Yamauchi, I’d call them back later. But if it were Horikita…I’d have to think about it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He has no scene of his own in the second half of Chapter 4; both mentions are the class&#x27;s assumptions about him rather than anything he does.<span class=\"pg\">p.129–148<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p79-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.1: he has the only confident opinion of Sakura, and it is invented<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p167-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.3: the magazine fight<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p167-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"","w":"yamauchi-haruki","q":"yamauchi haruki ch 5  5 3  the magazine fight  ike and yamauchi scrambled over a weekly manga magazine  during the lunch strategy meeting  the exchange that follows has one untagged line  and the second speaker is not assigned here","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p167-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 §5.3: the magazine fight<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.167–168<\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> &quot;Ike and Yamauchi scrambled over a weekly manga magazine&quot; during the lunch strategy meeting; the exchange that follows has one untagged line, and the second speaker is not assigned here.<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p129-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.8, §4.11: he is a category in someone else&#x27;s phone etiquette<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p179-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.6: he half-sees it first<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p179-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"yamauchi-haruki","q":"yamauchi haruki ch 5  5 6  he half sees it first the narration marks him as persuaded before ike   ike laughed  but yamauchi s expression stiffened   hey  ike  you know  when i actually get a good look at her  i think she probably does look a little like sakura   those are simplistic ways to identify somebody","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p179-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 §5.6: he half-sees it first<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.179–180<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Hey, Ike… You know, when I actually get a good look at her, I…think she probably does look a little like Sakura.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Those are simplistic ways to identify somebody…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The narration marks him as persuaded before Ike: &quot;Ike laughed, but Yamauchi’s expression stiffened.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p167-1\">← Before: Ch.5 §5.3: the magazine fight<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p190-1\">→ After: Ch.6 open: the look he cannot stop<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p190-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"","w":"yamauchi-haruki","q":"yamauchi haruki ch 6 open  the look he cannot stop he and ike watch sakura on the morning of the hearing because  they now knew of her idol identity  the narrator watches the watching  and notes that sakura guessed it  oh no  before anyone said anything  the chapter 5 doubt he voiced   that sakura looked a little like the idol   has been settled off the page  he gets no line here  only the glance","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p190-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 open: the look he cannot stop<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.190<\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He and Ike watch Sakura on the morning of the hearing because &quot;they now knew of her idol identity&quot;; the narrator watches the watching, and notes that Sakura guessed it &quot;Oh no…&quot; before anyone said anything.<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The Chapter 5 doubt he voiced — that Sakura looked a little like the idol — has been settled off the page; he gets no line here, only the glance.<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p179-1\">← Before: Ch.5 §5.6: he half-sees it first<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v3-p13-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"","w":"ike-kanji sakura-airi ayanokouji-kiyotaka ibuki-mio yamauchi-haruki","q":"yamauchi haruki ch 2  2 0 2 8  the target switch  the matches  and bringing ibuki in deck of the liner  insults sudou about his near expulsion while sudou laughs it off  goes oddly quiet during ike s kushida campaign  never raises the subject again  confides the plan in a whisper    i think i m gonna go for sakura    framing her as the reachable backup after kushida  asks ayanokoji to leave him alone with her  gets refused and recovers instantly    jeez  you re stiff  well  fine  burns three matches and gets only smoke  runs off to ask the teacher and comes back to ike s finished fire  the one who won t walk past the swollen cheeked class c girl  insists the three of them wait until she moves  explains her situation to the class when sato notices the interloper  maps the girls  teams for the boys    the empress team  led by karuizawa  kushida chan s friendship team  shinohara s arrogant team  then you have horikita and sakura  who are by themselves    and wants to eat with the last of them","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v3-p13-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.0–§2.8: the target-switch, the matches, and bringing Ibuki in<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.13–17, p.73–98<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Deck of the liner; insults Sudou about his near-expulsion while Sudou laughs it off.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Goes oddly quiet during Ike&#x27;s Kushida campaign; never raises the subject again.<span class=\"pg\">p.16–17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Confides the plan in a whisper — &quot;I think…I’m gonna go for Sakura&quot; — framing her as the reachable backup after Kushida; asks Ayanokōji to leave him alone with her.<span class=\"pg\">p.73–77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Gets refused and recovers instantly — &quot;Jeez, you’re stiff. Well, fine.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Burns three matches and gets only smoke; runs off to ask the teacher and comes back to Ike&#x27;s finished fire.<span class=\"pg\">p.83–84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> The one who won&#x27;t walk past the swollen-cheeked Class C girl; insists the three of them wait until she moves.<span class=\"pg\">p.80–82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Explains her situation to the class when Satō notices the interloper.<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Maps the girls&#x27; teams for the boys — &quot;the Empress Team, led by Karuizawa… Kushida-chan’s Friendship Team… Shinohara’s Arrogant Team. Then you have Horikita and Sakura, who are by themselves&quot; — and wants to eat with the last of them.<span class=\"pg\">p.96–97<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v3-p141-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.3: the shirtless accusation<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v3-p141-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"sakura-airi ike-kanji ayanokouji-kiyotaka yamauchi-haruki","q":"yamauchi haruki ch 4  4 3  the shirtless accusation dashes over when ike calls  grabs his arm and shoves him away from sakura   h h hey  you  why were you all alone and shirtless with sakura  why  huh  the whole challenge is the pairing   he puts himself between them in front of the camp  answers the call straight into the rant   i trusted you  ayanokouji  rants and raves while he goes off to report to hirata  the accusation is never answered","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v3-p141-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.3: the shirtless accusation<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.141–142<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Dashes over when Ike calls, grabs his arm and shoves him away from Sakura.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“H-h-hey, you! Why were you all alone and shirtless with Sakura?! Why?! Huh?!”<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I trusted you, Ayanokouji!”<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> The whole challenge is the pairing — he puts himself between them in front of the camp.<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Answers the call straight into the rant.<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Rants and raves while he goes off to report to Hirata; the accusation is never answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v3-p13-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.0–§2.8: the target-switch, the matches, and bringing Ibuki in<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v3-p159-1\">→ After: Ch.6: the bag search<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v3-p159-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"ike-kanji yamauchi-haruki","q":"yamauchi haruki ch 6  the bag search backs the boys  protest  then is the one who snatches ike s bag and finds the underwear   exactly  it s not like we stole karuizawa s underwear or anything  the translation leaves the line untagged  the narration then follows him exchanging looks with everyone   what  you re the one that really stole them   wait  don t tell me  snatches his bag on suspicion and finds the planted underwear inside   no  i m not saying that  show me what s in your bag   come on  don t give me that excuse   this is shameful  let s go explain things to hirata and the others   there was no culprit right   well  that sounds right  but  wait  what  you mean someone put the underwear in kanji s bag  apologizes and hurries away  leaving ayanokoji holding the evidence  stands still through the pat down  nothing is found on him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v3-p159-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6: the bag search<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.159–170<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Backs the boys’ protest, then is the one who snatches Ike’s bag and finds the underwear.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Exactly. It’s not like we stole Karuizawa’s underwear or anything.”<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“What, you’re the one that really stole them?”<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Wait, don’t tell me…”<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The translation leaves the line untagged; the narration then follows him exchanging looks with everyone.<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Snatches his bag on suspicion and finds the planted underwear inside.<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, I’m not saying that. Show me what’s in your bag.”<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Come on, don’t give me that excuse…”<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This is shameful. Let’s go explain things to Hirata and the others.”<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There was no culprit…right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, that sounds right, but… Wait, what? You mean someone put the underwear in Kanji’s bag?”<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Apologizes and hurries away, leaving Ayanokōji holding the evidence.<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Stands still through the pat-down; nothing is found on him.<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v3-p141-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.3: the shirtless accusation<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v3-p171-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6.1: volunteering<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v3-p171-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"yamauchi-haruki","q":"yamauchi haruki ch 6  6 1  volunteering raises his hand for the girls  physical work the moment hirata asks for another boy   wait  if you re looking for the guy with the skills  then i m your man  whatever the heat of the argument with the girls  he still wants to get closer to them  feigned ignorance with ike when the girls turned on ayanokoji","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v3-p171-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6.1: volunteering<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.171–178<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Raises his hand for the girls’ physical work the moment Hirata asks for another boy.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Wait. If you’re looking for the guy with the skills, then I’m your man!”<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Whatever the heat of the argument with the girls, he still wants to get closer to them.<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Feigned ignorance with Ike when the girls turned on Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v3-p159-1\">← Before: Ch.6: the bag search<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v3-p194-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6.4: the mud bribe<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v3-p194-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"sakura-airi kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka yamauchi-haruki","q":"yamauchi haruki ch 6  6 4  the mud bribe happy that ibuki joined  he eyes sakura through the forest   and ends up bribed into smearing mud on horikita s hair   hey  that s great  that s great  you know  this kinda feels like a harem or something  tries to talk to her kindly while staring at her chest   aren t you hot  sakura   karuizawa was so mean yesterday  wasn t she  and even though you were being so kind by sticking up for ayanokouji  sakura  is given treetop duty by ayanokoji to keep his eyes off sakura   what s the matter  kushida chan   good question  why are you two close  anyway   wh what re yuh doin  gets slapped by horikita for peering into her face  then takes kushida s hand to stand   ha ha  s sorry  yamauchi kun  i started trouble  are you okay   y you re so kind  kushida   wh what s the thing in common that you noticed  kushida   did she dump you  asks whether horikita dumped him  then is bribed with sakura s e mail address   what is it  you know my love consultation fee is high  right   huh  b but if i do something like that  i ll be killed  no way   listen here  dude  no matter how angry you say you are at horikita  trying to get revenge on her is uncool","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v3-p194-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6.4: the mud bribe<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.194–199<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Happy that Ibuki joined, he eyes Sakura through the forest — and ends up bribed into smearing mud on Horikita’s hair.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Hey, that’s great, that’s great! You know, this kinda feels like a harem or something!”<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Aren’t you hot, Sakura?”<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Karuizawa was so mean yesterday, wasn’t she? And even though you were being so kind by sticking up for Ayanokouji, Sakura.”<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>14 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Tries to talk to her kindly while staring at her chest.<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Is given treetop duty by Ayanokōji to keep his eyes off Sakura.<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What’s the matter, Kushida-chan?”<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Good question. Why are you two close, anyway?”<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wh-what’re yuh doin’?!”<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Gets slapped by Horikita for peering into her face, then takes Kushida’s hand to stand.<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ha ha… S-sorry, Yamauchi-kun. I started trouble. Are you okay?”<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Y-you’re so kind, Kushida…”<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wh-what’s the thing in common that you noticed, Kushida?”<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Did she dump you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Asks whether Horikita dumped him, then is bribed with Sakura’s e-mail address.<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What is it? You know my love consultation fee is high, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Huh? B-but if I do something like that, I’ll be killed! No way!”<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Listen here, dude. No matter how angry you say you are at Horikita, trying to get revenge on her is uncool!”<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v3-p171-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6.1: volunteering<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v3-p200-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6.5: paid in full<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v3-p200-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ike-kanji yamauchi-haruki","q":"yamauchi haruki ch 6  6 5  paid in full delivers the bribe  mud over horikita s hair in exchange for sakura s address   s sakura s e mail address  man  i i guess i have to do this now  huh   ha ha ha ha  you re all covered in mud  horikita  hilarious  points and laughs straight into the throw   horikita grabs his arm and puts him down without a word  gets her lifetime grudge line for the mud  she throws him before the whole camp   i  i  i d did it  s so  you have to keep your promise  beaten black and blue  he cowers behind ayanokoji while horikita threatens him   i m going to rest for a bit  the parts where i got punched really hurt  hobbles into the tent weeping after the job   hey kanji  i can t see ibuki anywhere  reports the missing ibuki and bag to ike first as the suspicion turns","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v3-p200-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6.5: paid in full<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.200–202<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Delivers the bribe: mud over Horikita’s hair in exchange for Sakura’s address.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“S-Sakura’s e-mail address? Man! I-I guess I have to do this now, huh?”<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Ha ha ha ha! You’re all covered in mud, Horikita! Hilarious!”<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I, I, I d-did it! S-so, you have to keep your promise!”<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Points and laughs straight into the throw — Horikita grabs his arm and puts him down without a word.<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Gets her lifetime-grudge line for the mud; she throws him before the whole camp.<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Beaten black and blue, he cowers behind Ayanokōji while Horikita threatens him.<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m going to rest for a bit. The parts where I got punched really hurt…”<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Hobbles into the tent weeping after the job.<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hey Kanji, I can’t see Ibuki anywhere.”<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Reports the missing Ibuki and bag to Ike first as the suspicion turns.<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v3-p194-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6.4: the mud bribe<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v3-p240-1\">→ After: Ch.7: the trio and the mud bribe<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v3-p240-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune yamauchi-haruki","q":"yamauchi haruki ch 7  the trio and the mud bribe stands with sudou and ike at the rest area  then turns up in the lounge retelling as the opening that let ibuki take the card   did you drop the card on purpose back then  well  i suppose that yamauchi kun s actions might have provided ibuki san the opportunity to hatch a plan to steal the keycard  the mud bribe she took read back as the opening that let ibuki take the card","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v3-p240-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7: the trio and the mud bribe<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.240, p.254<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Stands with Sudou and Ike at the rest area, then turns up in the lounge retelling as the opening that let Ibuki take the card.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “Did you drop the card on purpose back then? Well, I suppose that Yamauchi-kun’s actions might have provided Ibuki-san the opportunity to hatch a plan to steal the keycard…”<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The mud bribe she took read back as the opening that let Ibuki take the card.<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v3-p200-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6.5: paid in full<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4-p19-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"yamauchi-haruki","q":"yamauchi haruki ch 2  2 0  a hypothetical at the deck restaurant named once  hypothetically   what he and ike would have done at the deck restaurant  ayanokoji s aside  had they been there  they would have  foregone the food and feasted their eyes on the girls instead","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4-p19-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.0: a hypothetical at the deck restaurant<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.19<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named once, hypothetically — what he and Ike would have done at the deck restaurant.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ayanokōji’s aside: had they been there, they would have “foregone the food and feasted their eyes on the girls instead.”<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4-p101-1\">→ After: Ch.3: asked after<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4-p101-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"yamauchi-haruki","q":"yamauchi haruki ch 3  asked after named in a check on whether he had contacted anyone since the discussion ended  the question whether yamauchi has gotten in touch since the discussion ended is answered  no  he hasn t   and the reply asks whether something is the matter","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4-p101-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: asked after<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.101<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in a check on whether he had contacted anyone since the discussion ended.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The question whether Yamauchi has gotten in touch since the discussion ended is answered: no, he hasn’t — and the reply asks whether something is the matter.<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4-p19-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.0: a hypothetical at the deck restaurant<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4-p103-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.3: the neck-grab and the camera stimulus<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4-p103-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka sakura-airi yamauchi-haruki","q":"yamauchi haruki ch 3  3 3  the neck grab and the camera stimulus ambushes ayanokoji inside the ship over sakura s email  nearly chokes him  then walks out of the cabin door with a mission  grabs ayanokoji from behind and tightens on his neck until he taps out    looking like some sort of oni or an asura   what s the matter  my ass  you said you d tell me sakura s email address  for chrissakes  and you were talking with sakura just now  i knew it  you were after her all along  he shouted   wait  you lied   so  wait  so just now you were trying to ask sakura for her email address   so  you didn t know her email address at all  ayanokouji  you lied to me  he sputtered   so how d it go  did you get sakura s email address   sorry  what does that mean  i m not looking for an apology  i m looking for her email  yamauchi muttered to himself  reflecting the depth of his disappointment   how are you  how dare you trick me  he shouted   more time   show me a liar and i will show you a thief  he shouted   the proverb that shocks the narrator   yeah  that s right   on making sakura tell him   probably blinded by anger  willing to get the contact by force   you mean guys like you  ayanokouji  he shouted   on sakura hating guys that are all talk   you re just making excuses  you never knew her info in the first place  yamauchi lowered his head   but what the hell should i do  he asked   oh  she d be happy  for sure  but i don t have any points  either   so if i do my best  there s a chance i can get a new camera for sakura  he asked  yamauchi was about to burst   i ll do it  i ll do it  i ll do it  i ll do it  i ll give it everything i ve got and win sakura  he shouted   yeah  i m definitely going to win  he shouted   what  he asked   when ayanokoji starts  let me tell you something  just in case   of course   on not letting other classes beat him to the vip  blinded by anger at first  then coachable the moment the camera and points route appears  the narrator redirected his energy into the test as a temporary fix and worries he might fire past the target  the liar  then the coach  the crush whose email and camera drive every line he speaks","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4-p103-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 §3.3: the neck-grab and the camera stimulus<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.103–105<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ambushes Ayanokōji inside the ship over Sakura’s email, nearly chokes him, then walks out of the cabin door with a mission.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“‘What’s the matter’ my ass! You said you’d tell me Sakura’s email address, for chrissakes! And you were talking with Sakura just now! I knew it. You were after her all along!” he shouted.<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Wait. You lied?”<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“So… Wait, so just now you were trying to ask Sakura for her email address?”<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>18 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Grabs Ayanokōji from behind and tightens on his neck until he taps out — “looking like some sort of oni or an asura.”<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So… You didn’t know her email address at all, Ayanokouji. You lied to me?” he sputtered.<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So how’d it go? Did you get Sakura’s email address?”<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sorry? What does that mean? I’m not looking for an apology, I’m looking for her email!” Yamauchi muttered to himself, reflecting the depth of his disappointment. “How are you… How dare you trick me!” he shouted.<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “More time?! ‘Show me a liar and I will show you a thief’!” he shouted. (the proverb that shocks the narrator)<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah, that’s right.” (on making Sakura tell him — probably blinded by anger, willing to get the contact by force)<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You mean guys like you, Ayanokouji?!” he shouted. (on Sakura hating guys that are all talk)<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re just making excuses. You never knew her info in the first place.” Yamauchi lowered his head.<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But what the hell should I do?” he asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh, she’d be happy, for sure, but…I don’t have any points, either.”<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So if I do my best, there’s a chance I can get a new camera for Sakura?” he asked. Yamauchi was about to burst.<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll do it, I’ll do it, I’ll do it, I’ll do it! I’ll give it everything I’ve got and win Sakura!” he shouted.<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah! I’m definitely going to win!” he shouted.<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What?” he asked. (when Ayanokōji starts “Let me tell you something, just in case…”)<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course.” (on not letting other classes beat him to the VIP)<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Blinded by anger at first, then coachable the moment the camera-and-points route appears; the narrator redirected his energy into the test as a temporary fix and worries he might fire past the target.<span class=\"pg\">p.103–105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The liar, then the coach.<span class=\"pg\">p.103–105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> The crush whose email and camera drive every line he speaks.<span class=\"pg\">p.103–105<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4-p101-1\">← Before: Ch.3: asked after<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4-p179-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.4: the contrast name<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4-p179-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka yamauchi-haruki","q":"yamauchi haruki ch 4  4 4  the contrast name named with ike in hirata s compliment   ayanokoji is  different from ike kun and yamauchi kun  the comparison class for  amazing   i m worse than them    his self ranking under yamauchi  no scene presence  one name in hirata s line","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4-p179-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.4: the contrast name<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.179<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named with Ike in Hirata’s compliment — Ayanokōji is “different from Ike-kun and Yamauchi-kun.”<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> The comparison class for “amazing.”<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “I’m worse than them” — his self-ranking under Yamauchi.<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> No scene presence; one name in Hirata’s line.<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4-p103-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.3: the neck-grab and the camera stimulus<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4-p236-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.3: the Rooster who hesitated<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4-p236-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka yamauchi-haruki","q":"yamauchi haruki ch 5  5 3  the rooster who hesitated reported by horikita  rooster group  tried to send the betrayal email  agonized too long  test ended first  her report and her prediction he would have guessed wrong    the moment he hesitated to send that email  it was all over for him   he wasn t the cocksure guy he imagined himself to be    the reckless image broken by one hesitation   is yamauchi okay    asked and answered  no further stake  mention only  rooster s actual outcome  3 comes from the results list","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4-p236-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 §5.3: the Rooster who hesitated<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.236<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Reported by Horikita: Rooster group, tried to send the betrayal email, agonized too long, test ended first.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Her report and her prediction he would have guessed wrong — “the moment he hesitated to send that email, it was all over for him.”<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> “He wasn’t the cocksure guy he imagined himself to be” — the reckless image broken by one hesitation.<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Is Yamauchi okay?” — asked and answered; no further stake.<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Mention only; Rooster’s actual Outcome #3 comes from the results list.<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4-p179-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.4: the contrast name<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4_5-p13-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"","w":"yamauchi-haruki","q":"yamauchi haruki ch 2  a passing mention in the tournament call named when ayanokoji asks after him mid call  the answer comes back about the deleted exam data  the question  what about yamauchi  gets the answer about the data   the narration plans to confirm with him later that the deletion held","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4_5-p13-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: a passing mention in the tournament call<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.13<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named when Ayanokōji asks after him mid-call; the answer comes back about the deleted exam data.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The question “What about Yamauchi?” gets the answer about the data — the narration plans to confirm with him later that the deletion held.<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4_5-p28-1\">→ After: Ch.2: a passing mention in the partner list<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4_5-p28-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"","w":"yamauchi-haruki","q":"yamauchi haruki ch 2  a passing mention in the partner list named once among the guys who would not spend their last summer days on a paired reading  the list   the guys  like sudou  ike  and yamauchi    rejected without being asked","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4_5-p28-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: a passing mention in the partner list<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.28<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named once among the guys who would not spend their last summer days on a paired reading.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The list: “the guys, like Sudou, Ike, and Yamauchi” — rejected without being asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4_5-p13-1\">← Before: Ch.2: a passing mention in the tournament call<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4_5-p49-1\">→ After: Ch.3: the researcher of the group<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4_5-p49-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"spoken","w":"ike-kanji katsuragi-kouhei yamauchi-haruki","q":"yamauchi haruki ch 3  the researcher of the group yamauchi answers the birthday chat slowly  he has no money until next month   well  i don t got any money  he complains about shopping for a present he does not care about  then argues with ike over who must choose   now i have to shop for a present i don t even care about with a bunch of assholes  he knows inogashira likes the white bear series and rejects ak s phone case and screen protector picks   you really have no sense when it comes to this stuff  ayanokouji   kokoro chan likes the white bear series  so she should be happy with this present  he is the one who spots ike frozen at the shinohara keychains and presses him on it   if i remember correctly  didn t shinohara like that orange character   something seems super suspicious here  don t you think  ayanokouji  he spots katsuragi in the store and pulls ak over to watch   what s baldy got there  with ike he rushes to the shelf katsuragi bought from and works himself into jealous rage over the chocolate   w wait  don t tell me that baldy already has a girlfriend   who gives a present with such cute wrapping paper to a friend","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4_5-p49-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: the researcher of the group<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.49, 51–58<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Yamauchi answers the birthday chat slowly: he has no money until next month. He complains about shopping for a present he does not care about, then argues with Ike over who must choose. With Ike he rushes to the shelf Katsuragi bought from and works himself into jealous rage over the chocolate.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Well, I don’t got any money.”<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Now I have to shop for a present I don’t even care about with a bunch of assholes!”<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You really have no sense when it comes to this stuff, Ayanokouji.”<span class=\"pg\">p.53<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> He knows Inogashira likes the white bear series and rejects AK&#x27;s phone case and screen protector picks.<span class=\"pg\">p.52–53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Kokoro-chan likes the white bear series, so she should be happy with this present.”<span class=\"pg\">p.53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> He is the one who spots Ike frozen at the Shinohara keychains and presses him on it.<span class=\"pg\">p.53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If I remember correctly, didn’t Shinohara like that orange character?”<span class=\"pg\">p.53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Something seems super suspicious here, don’t you think, Ayanokouji?”<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> He spots Katsuragi in the store and pulls AK over to watch.<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What’s baldy got there?!”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “W-wait, don’t tell me that baldy already has a girlfriend?!”<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Who gives a present with such cute wrapping paper to a friend?!”<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4_5-p28-1\">← Before: Ch.2: a passing mention in the partner list<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4_5-p60-1\">→ After: Ch.3: on the sidelines in the room<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4_5-p60-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"spoken","w":"sudou-ken yamauchi-haruki","q":"yamauchi haruki ch 3  on the sidelines in the room present in ak s room for the birthday question  he laughs at ike in the headlock and later reminds sudou about his tournament   that reminds me  your tournament s coming up soon  he supplies the thursday tournament date that gives sudou his excuse not to investigate","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4_5-p60-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: on the sidelines in the room<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.60, 63–64<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Present in AK&#x27;s room for the birthday question; he laughs at Ike in the headlock and later reminds Sudou about his tournament.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“That reminds me, your tournament’s coming up soon,”<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> He supplies the Thursday tournament date that gives Sudou his excuse not to investigate.<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4_5-p49-1\">← Before: Ch.3: the researcher of the group<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4_5-p79-1\">→ After: Ch.3: the self-gift theory<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4_5-p79-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"spoken","w":"ike-kanji katsuragi-kouhei yamauchi-haruki","q":"yamauchi haruki ch 3  the self gift theory he supplies the theory that katsuragi bought the girlish chocolates for himself   i think he actually bought the gift for himself  sorrowful  not overjoyed  he opens with the junior high valentine s hell question  he and ike agree the class a leader s popularity is an act  ak refrains from commenting  he denies being the unpopular guy of his own story when ike jabs back   wrong  he just reminded me of my classmate  i felt sorry for him  he flips from hating katsuragi to liking him in two seconds and pushes the celebration","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4_5-p79-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: the self-gift theory<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.79–82<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">He supplies the theory that Katsuragi bought the girlish chocolates for himself.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I think he actually bought the gift for himself,”<span class=\"pg\">p.79<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Wrong. He just reminded me of my classmate. I felt sorry for him.”<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Voice<\/span> Sorrowful, not overjoyed: he opens with the junior-high Valentine&#x27;s hell question.<span class=\"pg\">p.79<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> He and Ike agree the Class A leader&#x27;s popularity is an act; AK refrains from commenting.<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> He denies being the unpopular guy of his own story when Ike jabs back.<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> He flips from hating Katsuragi to liking him in two seconds and pushes the celebration.<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4_5-p60-1\">← Before: Ch.3: on the sidelines in the room<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4_5-p83-1\">→ After: Ch.3: the celebration crew<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4_5-p83-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"","w":"kushida-kikyou yamauchi-haruki","q":"yamauchi haruki ch 3  the celebration crew he walks with the group to shop  happier with kushida present even though he is aiming for sakura  kushida s charms affect him too  the narration notes  with ike he ambushes katsuragi with party poppers and the melted cake  the second class d boy is never named on the page  the plan s pair makes him yamauchi   an inference  not a printed name","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4_5-p83-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: the celebration crew<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.83, 105<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">He walks with the group to shop, happier with Kushida present even though he is aiming for Sakura. With Ike he ambushes Katsuragi with party poppers and the melted cake.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Kushida&#x27;s charms affect him too, the narration notes.<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The second Class D boy is never named on the page; the plan&#x27;s pair makes him Yamauchi — an inference, not a printed name.<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4_5-p79-1\">← Before: Ch.3: the self-gift theory<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4_5-p132-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.1: the letter and the plan<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4_5-p132-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"action spoken","w":"sakura-airi yamauchi-haruki","q":"yamauchi haruki ch 5  5 1  the letter and the plan he bursts into ak s room on the last days of vacation to demand the day s obedience   you re gonna do what i say today  ayanokouji  the printed love letter carries all his feelings   and a monthly points tribute line   i ve written about just how much i love sakura   i m not really proud of this  but my handwriting sucks   starting with the second semester  i m aiming for my dream school life  he has already asked kushida to call sakura and wants ak to deliver the letter   i want you to deliver the letter   the last time i felt this nervous  i won the final match at the ryougoku kokugikan sumo hall  ak judges the kokugikan final a probable lie   weak and uncharacteristic   any past problems between us will all be water under the bridge  he wants the answer behind the school building after gym number two   a confession spot rumor   if you confess your feelings there  it s sure to go well   damn  i m so nervous   th that s impossible  dude   so  when you hand over the letter  don t mention me at all  panicked at sakura s footsteps  he hangs up and leaves the rest to ak   i m leaving the rest to you   how d she react   d don t use a scary word like  judgment   isn t that a sigh of love","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4_5-p132-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 §5.1: the letter and the plan<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.132–143<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">He bursts into AK&#x27;s room on the last days of vacation to demand the day&#x27;s obedience.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“You’re gonna do what I say today, Ayanokouji!”<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’ve written about just how much I love Sakura!”<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’m not really proud of this, but my handwriting sucks.”<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>17 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> The printed love letter carries all his feelings — and a monthly-points tribute line.<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Starting with the second semester, I’m aiming for my dream school life!”<span class=\"pg\">p.134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> He has already asked Kushida to call Sakura and wants AK to deliver the letter.<span class=\"pg\">p.134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I want you to deliver the letter.”<span class=\"pg\">p.134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The last time I felt this nervous, I won the final match at the Ryougoku Kokugikan Sumo Hall.”<span class=\"pg\">p.134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> AK judges the Kokugikan final a probable lie — weak and uncharacteristic.<span class=\"pg\">p.134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Any past problems between us will all be water under the bridge!”<span class=\"pg\">p.134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> He wants the answer behind the school building after Gym Number Two — a confession-spot rumor.<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you confess your feelings there, it’s sure to go well.”<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Damn, I’m so nervous!”<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Th-that’s impossible, dude.”<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So, when you hand over the letter, don’t mention me at all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Panicked at Sakura&#x27;s footsteps, he hangs up and leaves the rest to AK.<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m leaving the rest to you!”<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “How’d she react?!”<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “D-don’t use a scary word like ‘judgment’!”<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Isn’t that a sigh of love?”<span class=\"pg\">p.143<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4_5-p83-1\">← Before: Ch.3: the celebration crew<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4_5-p150-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.3: the rejection and the phone<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4_5-p150-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"action spoken","w":"sakura-airi ayanokouji-kiyotaka yamauchi-haruki","q":"yamauchi haruki ch 5  5 3  the rejection and the phone he arrives stiff for the answer and finds ak already there at sakura s request   wh why are you here  ayanokouji   so  did you read my letter   i like you  sakura   thank you  sakura  her careful rejection leaves him shocked but guilt free   i almost feel relieved  you know   i feel incredibly guilty   i didn t really love her  he concludes he was after face and body only  not love  and resolves to find a girl he really likes   i m grateful to you  ayanokouji  he lends ak a phone   the borrowed device ak asked for   as an exception to the confession contingent deal   i m making an exception   didn t you say it depended on your confession being successful  he runs off after sakura in the clearing rain","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4_5-p150-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 §5.3: the rejection and the phone<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.150–152<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">He arrives stiff for the answer and finds AK already there at Sakura&#x27;s request.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Wh-why are you here, Ayanokouji?”<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“So, did you read my letter?”<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I like you, Sakura!”<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Thank you, Sakura.”<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Her careful rejection leaves him shocked but guilt-free.<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I almost feel relieved, you know?”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I feel incredibly guilty.”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I didn’t really love her.”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> He concludes he was after face and body only, not love, and resolves to find a girl he really likes.<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m grateful to you, Ayanokouji.”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> He lends AK a phone — the borrowed device AK asked for — as an exception to the confession-contingent deal.<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m making an exception.”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Didn’t you say it depended on your confession being successful?”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> He runs off after Sakura in the clearing rain.<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4_5-p132-1\">← Before: Ch.5 §5.1: the letter and the plan<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4_5-p163-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6.1–6.4: the pool plot<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4_5-p163-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"action spoken","w":"yamauchi-haruki","q":"yamauchi haruki ch 6  6 1 6 4  the pool plot in the group chat he agrees the summer must not end like this   a fresh start after the rejection   no  it s not okay   invite sakura for me  please  i beg you  ayanokouji  he privately begs ak not to reveal the rejection  he goes up to wake sudou  escaping the awkward silence with sakura   yeah  we re going further than anyone in our class has gone   geh  what the hell  ken   whoa  awesome  this is  like  some next level stuff  huh  he stammers a question about the handsome volleyball player that runs off the page","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4_5-p163-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6.1–6.4: the pool plot<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.163–178<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">In the group chat he agrees the summer must not end like this — a fresh start after the rejection.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“No, it’s not okay!”<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Invite Sakura for me! Please, I beg you, Ayanokouji!”<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Yeah. We’re going further than anyone in our class has gone.”<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> He privately begs AK not to reveal the rejection.<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> He goes up to wake Sudou, escaping the awkward silence with Sakura.<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Geh! What the hell, Ken?”<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Whoa! Awesome! This is, like, some next-level stuff, huh?!”<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He stammers a question about the handsome volleyball player that runs off the page.<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4_5-p150-1\">← Before: Ch.5 §5.3: the rejection and the phone<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4_5-p187-1\">→ After: Ch.6: the death sentence<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4_5-p187-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"action spoken","w":"ike-kanji yamauchi-haruki","q":"yamauchi haruki ch 6  the death sentence yamauchi drops serves  copies ike s rude gesture  gets caught  and is knocked out by sudou after the match   gyah  sorry  shouted yamauchi   hey  haruki  you re gettin  the death sentence later   no way  no way  yamauchi gurgled  falling face down in the water   sudou s getting full of himself  said yamauchi  collapsed outside the pool  he glares at sudou after the promised knockout  he orders shaved ice at the convenience store  he copies ike s flipped finger at sudou and pays for it with the death sentence","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4_5-p187-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6: the death sentence<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.187–200<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Yamauchi drops serves, copies Ike&#x27;s rude gesture, gets caught, and is knocked out by Sudou after the match.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Gyah! Sorry!” shouted Yamauchi.<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Hey, Haruki. You&#x27;re gettin&#x27; the death sentence later.”<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“No way, no way!” Yamauchi gurgled, falling face down in the water.<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sudou&#x27;s getting full of himself,” said Yamauchi.<span class=\"pg\">p.189<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Collapsed outside the pool, he glares at Sudou after the promised knockout.<span class=\"pg\">p.189<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> He orders shaved ice at the convenience store.<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> He copies Ike&#x27;s flipped finger at Sudou and pays for it with the death sentence.<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4_5-p163-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6.1–6.4: the pool plot<\/button><\/div><\/article>"}];
